The bug occurs because a new hugetlb page allocated during the fallocate operation is not marked as active (using `set_page_huge_active`). This leads to a failure in the page migration code when it attempts to isolate the page, resulting in unexpected behavior. The lack of marking the page as active prevents proper management of the page's state during migration.

