Reason:
The bug occurs because after allocating a new hugetlb page during the fallocate operation, the page is not marked as active using `set_page_huge_active(page)`. This omission prevents the page from being properly managed during migration, leading to a failure when the migration code attempts to isolate the page.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
set_page_huge_active(page);
```
Reason:
The addition of `set_page_huge_active(page);` marks the newly allocated hugetlb page as active, ensuring that it is correctly managed during migration. This change resolves the issue of the page not being recognized as active, thus preventing the unexpected failure in the page migration code.


